# Multi-Tier Licensing Architecture — Farm Omni Gateway

To ensure complete legal rigor, prevent license conflicts between the Linux kernel and user-space applications, and provide reciprocal protection for physical hardware designs, **Farm Omni Gateway** adopts a **Multi-Tier Licensing Architecture by Layer**:

```text
farm-omni-gw/
├── hardware/              --> CERN-OHL-S v2 (Strongly Reciprocal Open Hardware)
│   └── LICENSE
├── os/                    --> GPL-2.0 (OpenWrt & Linux Mainline Kernel Boundary)
│   └── LICENSE
├── software/              --> AGPL-v3 (GNU Affero GPL for Applications, Daemons & Twin Models)
│   └── LICENSE
└── LICENSE                --> Master Multi-Tier Licensing Declaration
```

---

## 1. Layer Licensing Summary

| Layer & Directory | Target Assets | Governing License | SPDX Identifier | Rationale |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| [**`hardware/`**](./hardware/) | Schematics, PCB layouts, BOM, mechanical CAD, 3D enclosures | **CERN-OHL-S v2** | `CERN-OHL-S-2.0` | Prevents proprietary hardware cloning; mandates sharing of modified hardware designs. |
| [**`os/`**](./os/) | Kernel patches, device tree (DTS), OpenWrt configs, drivers | **GNU GPL v2.0** | `GPL-2.0-only` | Strictly respects the upstream Linux kernel license without GPL-v2/v3 conflicts. |
| [**`software/`**](./software/) | Onboarding portal, telemetry daemons, RTK caster, digital twin schemas | **GNU Affero GPL v3.0** | `AGPL-3.0-or-later` | Ensures copyleft protection across network and IoT services; prevents closed SaaS appropriation. |

---

## 2. Full License Texts

Detailed license texts are available in their respective subdirectories:
- Hardware: [**`hardware/LICENSE`**](./hardware/LICENSE)
- Operating System & Kernel: [**`os/LICENSE`**](./os/LICENSE)
- Software & Daemons: [**`software/LICENSE`**](./software/LICENSE)

Below are the declarations of the respective licenses:

### A. Hardware (`CERN-OHL-S-2.0`)
Copyright (C) 2026 Quatrain Technologies and Contributors.
Licensed under the CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Strongly Reciprocal.
You may redistribute and modify this documentation and hardware designs under the terms of the CERN-OHL-S v2.

### B. Operating System & Linux Kernel (`GPL-2.0-only`)
